{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass on the day that HaShem spoke to Moses in the land of Egypt</b> — It is reasonable to explain that the verse reverts to above, saying: this <b>\"and it came to pass\"</b> — that they were the ones speaking to Pharaoh king of Egypt — was at the time when <b>HaShem spoke to Moses in the land of Egypt</b>. For because it said, \"He is Aaron and Moses, to whom HaShem said, Bring out the children of Israel from the land of Egypt,\" it would have appeared that the speech was to both of them equally; now it explains that the speech was to Moses, while the command was to both of them, that they should bring them out. This is the reason for the break of the parashah division."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:04:35.853040316Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}